        ))}\n   128→              </div>\n   129→            </div>\n   130→          )}\n   131→\n   132→          {/* Supporting Sources */}\n   133→          {supportingSources.length > 0 && (\n   134→            <div className=\"bg-slate-50 rounded-md p-3 border-l-3 border-blue-400\">\n   135→              <div className=\"text-[10px] font-semibold text-blue-600 uppercase mb-2 flex items-center gap-1\">\n   136→                <span className=\"w-3 h-3\"><LinkIcon /></span>\n   137→                Sources ({supportingSources.length})\n   138→              </div>\n   139→              <div className=\"space-y-1\">\n   140→                {supportingSources.slice(0, 3).map((sourceId) => {\n   141→                  const source = sourceMap.get(sourceId);\n   142→                  if (!source) return null;\n   143→                  return (\n   144→                    <a\n   145→                      key={sourceId}\n   146→                      href={source.url}\n   147→                      target=\"_blank\"\n   148→                      rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\n   149→                      className=\"block text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline truncate\"\n   150→                    >\n   151→                      {source.title || source.domain || source.url}\n   152→                      {source.credibility_score && (\n   153→                        <span className=\"text-slate-400 ml-1\">\n   154→                          ({Math.round(source.credibility_score * 100)}% cred)\n   155→                        </span>\n   156→                      )}\n   157→                    </a>\n   158→                  );\n   159→                })}\n   160→              </div>\n   161→            </div>\n   162→          )}\n   163→        </div>\n   164→      )}\n   165→    </div>\n   166→  );\n   167→}\n   168→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what i